---
import TraversyLabLinks from '../../components/TraversyLabLinks.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Traversy Lab privacy policy"
  description="How Traversy Lab accesses, uses, stores, and shares Google user data."
  pageTitle="privacy.md"
  currentSection="legal"
>
  <TraversyLabLinks />

  <section class="section">
    <h1 class="h1"><span class="hash"># </span>Traversy Lab privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This policy explains how Traversy Lab handles Google user data for Brad
      Traversy's private personal automations.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">Effective: October 15, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>scope</h2>
    <p>
      Traversy Lab is a private system operated by Brad Traversy. It is not
      offered to the public. This policy applies to the Google accounts that
      Brad owns and explicitly authorizes for use with the system.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>Google data accessed</h2>
    <p>Traversy Lab requests read-only access to:</p>
    <ul class="prose-list">
      <li>basic account identity, including the authorized email address</li>
      <li>Gmail messages, threads, metadata, and labels</li>
      <li>Google Calendar events and their details</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The system does not request permission to send, modify, archive, label,
      or delete email. It does not request permission to create, modify, or
      delete calendar events.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>how the data is used</h2>
    <p>Google user data is used only to:</p>
    <ul class="prose-list">
      <li>mirror upcoming events into a private planning note</li>
      <li>surface relevant calendar and email items in a private morning briefing</li>
      <li>identify and track qualified sponsorship inquiries</li>
      <li>operate, secure, and troubleshoot those workflows</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Use of information received from Google APIs follows the Google API
      Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>storage and retention</h2>
    <p>
      OAuth credentials are stored in a protected credential store on a
      privately managed machine. They are not stored on this website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Selected event details, message summaries, qualified lead details, and
      workflow results may be stored in Brad's private local notes for as long
      as they remain useful. Traversy Lab does not create a general backup of a
      Gmail inbox or Google Calendar.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>sharing and disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      Some workflows use third-party AI services to summarize or classify
      content. Only the content needed to run the requested workflow is sent to
      those services. Traversy Lab does not sell Google user data, provide it to
      data brokers, or share it for advertising, credit, or marketing purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data may also be disclosed when required by law or when necessary to
      protect the security of the system, the authorized accounts, or other
      people.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>security</h2>
    <p>
      Traversy Lab uses reasonable technical and operational safeguards for
      credentials, Google user data, and stored workflow output. No system can
      guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>revoking access and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      The authorized account owner can revoke Traversy Lab's access from the{' '}
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" class="link">
        Google Account connections page
      </a>. Revocation stops future access but does not automatically delete
      existing private workflow output. To request deletion of retained output,
      email <a href="mailto:travxlabs@gmail.com" class="link">travxlabs@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="h2"><span class="hash">## </span>changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      This policy will be updated if Traversy Lab's use of Google user data
      changes. Questions can be sent to{' '}
      <a href="mailto:travxlabs@gmail.com" class="link">travxlabs@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="comment">
    // EOF privacy.md<span class="cursor"></span>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .meta {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--fg-comment);
    font-size: 12.5px;
  }

  .prose-list {
    margin: 12px 0 16px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    list-style: disc;
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .prose-list li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
